 "answer": {
  "answer": "Only one combination is confirmed as challenging, so the goal of 5 was not met. On scene 19f339ba, with the car 0.5 s earlier, the car at 1.25x speed and the ego at 1.4x (S26), every run failed. In each one the policy braked hard on an open highway for no visible reason, drifted left and struck a car coming up in the left lane. Three more scenes each have a strong candidate whose range does not yet clear 0.5: 187e6244 (S23), 023b7fcc (S1) and 1c45ce3a (S28, resting on only two runs). On 023b7fcc and 187e6244 the policy drifted left into the next lane against a RIGHT command. Most failures on 1c45ce3a were replayed cars cutting into a gap the human had already cleared, so they may not be the policy's fault. No scene gave a lead-vehicle braking failure or a departure from the road, and the other six scenes did not fail in the few runs each got.",
  "findings": [
   {
    "claim": "The one confirmed challenging case: on 19f339ba, with the car 0.5 s earlier at 1.25x and the ego at 1.4x, every run failed. In every run the policy was at fault. It braked hard with no lead car within about 45 m, drifted left and hit actor 1 coming up in the left lane.",
    "settings": [
     "S26"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 187e6244, the car 0.5 s later at 0.75x with the ego at 0.8x failed in most runs, but the range's lower end sits just under 0.5. Most of these failures were the policy steering left out of its lane against a RIGHT command and sideswiping car 7. One was car 7 drifting into the ego's left rear, where fault is unclear.",
    "settings": [
     "S23"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 023b7fcc, the car 0.5 s earlier at 1.0x with the ego slowed to 0.6x failed in most runs, but it is not yet confirmed above 0.5. Every failure was the policy's fault. The ego sped up, drifted about 2 m left of the human path against a RIGHT command, and made side contact with actor 56 in the left lane.",
    "settings": [
     "S1"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "The same knob values did not fail on 187e6244, so the 023b7fcc failure depends on the scene, not just the setting.",
    "settings": [
     "S1",
     "S21"
    ]
   },
   {
    "claim": "On 1c45ce3a, failures appeared at several settings with the ego at 0.8x, but triage puts little of the blame on the policy. In most of them a replayed car (actor 24, once actor 14) cut across the lane line into the ego's front-right corner, at a moment when the slowed ego sat about 8\u201320 m behind where the human had been. Triage rated fault unclear or not the policy's. S28 failed in both of its runs, but that is a hint, not a rate.",
    "settings": [
